WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.707 --> 00:00:11.710
The five assessments build one Personal Cartography across the term. These pages explain the arc, the rooms, the marking, the dates, and the AI rules, so the blank page never wins.

2
00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:21.419
Read the overview first. Five assignments, each worth 20 percent, move through one arc: notice, interpret, investigate, repair, and integrate.

3
00:00:21.419 --> 00:00:32.178
Open one assignment room at a time. Each room shows what you are really doing, what to submit, the marking criteria, and a final self-check with common misses.

4
00:00:32.178 --> 00:00:40.024
Check How Stronger Work Grows. The grading page shows what stronger work does, so you can aim before you submit.

5
00:00:40.024 --> 00:00:49.668
Confirm dates on the release page. It lists when each Blackboard dropbox opens and when work is due. Nothing is due in Study Week or Week 14.

6
00:00:49.668 --> 00:01:00.670
Open the Assignment Start Lab when you want a working session. It turns your assignment, progress, sticking point, and available time into a private start plan you can print or save. For Compass Check it builds readiness steps only and never generates or rehearses graded answers.

7
00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:08.951
Read the AI page before you disclose. It gives the AI-use rules clearly, with honest disclosure examples you can adapt.

8
00:01:08.951 --> 00:01:18.348
Submit on Blackboard, always. This site helps you start and plan. The official assignment, rubric, and submission all live on Blackboard.

9
00:01:18.348 --> 00:01:24.153
Nothing here is submitted or graded. Blackboard is the only submission channel.

10
00:01:24.153 --> 00:01:29.023
Where next: Block one hour, open the lab, and leave with a plan.
